What is Stack?
Ans: Stack is a data structure which works on LIFO mechanism, Last In First Out 

What is Queue?
Ans: Queue is a data structure which works on FIFO mechanism, First In First Out

1)Implementation of Stacks using Arrays
=====================================

To define arrays we want size ,size is mandatory . For this implementation size must be known . It can't be dynamic

code: public class practice{
    int st[] = new int[10];
    int top = -1;

    void push(int x){
        if(top>=9){
            System.out.println("Stack Overflow");
            return;
        }
        top=top+1;
        st[top]=x;
    }

    int top(){
        if(top==-1) return -1;
        return st[top];
    }

    void pop(){
        if(top==-1) {
            System.out.println("No element in stack");
            return;
        }
        top=top-1;
    }

    void display()
    {
        if(top == -1){
            System.out.println("Stack is empty");
            return;
        }
        int temp = top;
        while(temp>=0){
            System.out.print(st[temp]+" ");
            temp--;
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        practice s = new practice();
        s.push(10);
        s.push(20);
        s.push(30);
        s.push(40);
        s.push(50);
        s.display();
    }
}

2)Implementation of Queue using Arrays
======================================

public class practice{
    int size = 10;
    int[] queue = new int[size];
    int start = -1, end = -1, currSize = 0;

    void push(int x){
        if(currSize==size){
            System.out.println("Queue is full");
            return;
        }
        else if(currSize==0){
            start = 0;
            end = 0;
        }
        else{
            end = (end+1)%size;
        }

        queue[end]=x;
        currSize+=1;

    }

    int pop(){
        if(currSize==0){
            System.out.println("Queue is Empty");
            return -1;
        }
        int el = queue[start];
        if(currSize==1){
            start=-1;
            end=-1;
        }
        else{
            start=(start+1)%size;
        }
        currSize-=1;
        return el;
    }

    int top(){
        if(currSize==0){
            System.out.println("No element in Queue");
            return -1;
        }
        return queue[start];
    }

    int size(){
        return currSize;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        practice q = new practice();
        q.push(10);
        q.push(20);
        System.out.println(q.top());
    }
}

3)Implement Stack using two queue

code: class MyStack {
    Queue<Integer> q1 = new LinkedList<>();//Main queue
    Queue<Integer> q2 = new LinkedList<>();//Helper queue
    public MyStack() {
        
    }
    
    public void push(int x) {
        while(!q1.isEmpty())
        {
            q2.offer(q1.peek());
            q1.poll();
        }
        q1.offer(x);
        while(!q2.isEmpty())
        {
            q1.offer(q2.peek());
            q2.poll();
        }
    }
    
    public int pop() {
        int ans = q1.peek();
        q1.poll();
        return ans;
    }
    
    public int top() {
        return q1.peek();
    }
    
    public boolean empty() {
        return q1.isEmpty();
    }
}

jab push kar rahe hai tab ek queue as a helper use kar rahe hai , push karne se pehle helper queue mein daal rahe hai .
Uske baad element push karke , helper se nikal ke main queue mein daal denge . bas done implementation.

Implement Stack using Single queue

code: class MyStack {
    Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<>();
    public MyStack() {
        
    }
    
    public void push(int x) {
        q.offer(x);
        for(int i=0;i<q.size()-1;i++)
        {
            q.offer(q.peek());
            q.poll();
        }
    }
    
    public int pop() {
        return q.poll();
    }
    
    public int top() {
        return q.peek();
    }
    
    public boolean empty() {
        return q.isEmpty();
    }
}

